   "source": [
    "# Credit Card Default Prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal:** Understand the full data analyst / credit strategy function end-to-end\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset:** UCI \"Default of Credit Card Clients\" — download from Kaggle, save `UCI_Credit_Card.csv` in this same folder.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "1. Load & explore (EDA)\n",
    "2. Prepare data (features/label, train/test split)\n",
    "3. Train a model\n",
    "4. Evaluate properly (beyond accuracy)\n",
    "5. See overfitting for real\n",
    "6. Feature importance\n",
    "7. Turn probability into a DECISION (threshold)\n",
    "8. Expected loss & profit per customer\n",
    "9. Portfolio view\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 — Load & Explore (EDA)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why this matters:** Before any modelling, you must understand your data. The single most important thing here: *what fraction of customers actually defaulted?* This is the class balance, and it shapes everything.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Guiding questions to answer in your head:**\n",
    "- What is the default rate? (the target column is `default.payment.next.month`)\n",
    "- Is this balanced or imbalanced?\n",
    "- What features do you have, and are they all usable at *decision time* (i.e. before you approve someone)?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Index(['ID', 'LIMIT_BAL', 'SEX', 'EDUCATION', 'MARRIAGE', 'AGE', 'PAY_0',\n",
       "       'PAY_2', 'PAY_3', 'PAY_4', 'PAY_5', 'PAY_6', 'BILL_AMT1', 'BILL_AMT2',\n",
       "       'BILL_AMT3', 'BILL_AMT4', 'BILL_AMT5', 'BILL_AMT6', 'PAY_AMT1',\n",
       "       'PAY_AMT2', 'PAY_AMT3', 'PAY_AMT4', 'PAY_AMT5', 'PAY_AMT6',\n",
       "       'default.payment.next.month'],\n",
       "      dtype='object')"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 18,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
