   "source": [
    "## Step 4 — Evaluate Properly (the heart of the learning)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why this matters:** Accuracy LIES on imbalanced data. You need precision, recall, and AUC/Gini.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Precision:** of those the model flagged as defaulters, how many really defaulted?\n",
    "- **Recall:** of all real defaulters, how many did the model catch?\n",
    "- **AUC-ROC:** how well the model separates the two classes overall. In credit, **Gini = 2×AUC − 1** is the standard metric — know this term.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The trade-off:** catching more defaulters (high recall) usually means more false alarms (lower precision). Credit strategy is choosing where to sit on that trade-off.\n",
    "\n",
    "-Gini - > identify inequality"
   ]
  },
