    "## Step 8 — Expected Loss & Profit per Customer\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why this matters:** approving isn't about avoiding all risk — it's about PROFIT. A risky customer can still be profitable if priced right.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Simplified formulas (state your assumptions):**\n",
    "- Expected Loss = P(default) × Exposure × LGD  \n",
    "  (LGD = Loss Given Default, the fraction you lose if they default — assume e.g. 0.9)\n",
    "- Expected Revenue = Exposure × APR × (1 − P(default))  \n",
    "  (rough: you earn interest only if they don't default)\n",
    "- Expected Profit = Expected Revenue − Expected Loss\n",
    "\n",
    "Use `LIMIT_BAL` as a proxy for Exposure. These are simplifications — being able to SAY they're simplifications is itself a good interview signal."
   ]
